WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.370
As you can see, we took our show on the road today,

2
00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:06.300
or at least to the road, outside here,

3
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:09.400
from our studio on 57th Street in New York.

4
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:10.940
And it's time for a special

5
00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:13.043
outdoor edition of Cookbook Club!

6
00:00:17.090 --> 00:00:20.140
The notion that great barbecue only comes from the South

7
00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:23.580
was debunked by this former bodyguard

8
00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:25.930
turned pitmaster from Brooklyn.

9
00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:29.430
So here to show us how to switch up our Thanksgiving spread

10
00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:31.810
from the kitchen to the smoker,

11
00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:36.810
the owner of Hometown Barbecue, please welcome Billy Durney.

12
00:00:37.056 --> 00:00:38.494
(audience cheers)

13
00:00:38.494 --> 00:00:39.970
Hi Billy.
Thanks so much

14
00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:40.893
for having me today.

15
00:00:40.893 --> 00:00:43.560
Oh, I'm so glad that we could do this together.

16
00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:46.092
I'm so excited and I'm so excited to get you

17
00:00:46.092 --> 00:00:48.690
amongst our smoky little fire here.

18
00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:51.510
It's pretty perfect for the holiday.

19
00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:54.000
So the most successful turkey I ever made

20
00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.970
for Thanksgiving was brined.
Yes.

21
00:00:56.970 --> 00:01:00.200
And that is, I think, a crucial step

22
00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:04.230
in a very flavorful, juicy, amazing turkey.

23
00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:07.770
And I'm really excited to demo a brine,

24
00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:10.230
because sometimes when it's just words

25
00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:14.220
on a page or in a book, I am a very visual person.

26
00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:16.340
So that's why I even wanted to pour the water.

27
00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:19.130
'Cause sometimes I'm like, how much water are you talking?

28
00:01:19.130 --> 00:01:21.360
A bucket, a cup, what?

29
00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:22.790
Right, so for here we're gonna use

30
00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:26.600
a half a gallon or a gallon of water for one breast.

31
00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:28.170
So we could just throw that in over the turkey.

32
00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:29.003
Can we do that now?

33
00:01:29.003 --> 00:01:30.520
Yeah, we can just throw that in right over the turkey.

34
00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:31.840
So half of this?

35
00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:32.737
We can put the whole gallon in.

36
00:01:32.737 --> 00:01:34.063
All right, let's do it!

37
00:01:34.956 --> 00:01:35.789 line:15%
(audience cheers)

38
00:01:35.789 --> 00:01:37.010 line:15%
Yeah!

39
00:01:37.010 --> 00:01:40.140 line:15%
Beautiful, so it's fully submerged.

40
00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:41.390 line:15%
The turkey's fully submerged,

41
00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:42.967 line:15%
is basically what we're going for.

42
00:01:42.967 --> 00:01:46.490 line:15%
I'm a fully submerged turkey. (Billy laughs)

43
00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:48.540 line:15%
All right, so now, most brines start

44
00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:50.100 line:15%
really simply with salt and sugar.

45
00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:52.780
So we have sugar and salt, I would-

46
00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:54.054
And how much would you say?

47
00:01:54.054 --> 00:01:56.060
I would say a cup, so I'd say,

48
00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:59.870 line:15%
yeah, another little snudge.

49
00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:02.770 line:15%
I dunno if snudge is a word, but today it's a word.

50
00:02:02.770 --> 00:02:05.830 line:15%
All right, so like a generous cup.

51
00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:07.970
Generous cup, and then equal parts,

52
00:02:07.970 --> 00:02:10.220
I like to put equal parts, sugar and salt.

53
00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:14.600
And then we like whole peppercorn in ours.

54
00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:17.100 line:15%
I think the brine I did...

55
00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:18.692 line:15%
All of them?
No, no that's good.

56
00:02:18.692 --> 00:02:20.214 line:15%
That's good?
Yeah, about half a cup.

57
00:02:20.214 --> 00:02:22.410 line:15%
I think the one I did had like an anise?

58
00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:23.260
Yeah, anise is good.

59
00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:25.840
So a lot of people use juniper berry

60
00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:28.700
and like other floral things.

61
00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:30.140
But I like to keep it more savory

62
00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:31.430
and herby.
Yeah.

63
00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:34.277
And I love garlic, tons of garlic, so we could-

64
00:02:34.277 --> 00:02:35.110
Okay, the whole thing?

65
00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:36.400 line:15%
I would throw the whole-
Yeah!

66
00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:37.720 line:15%
I'm not messing around.
Let's do it!

67
00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:39.010 line:15%
Yeah!
Exactly.

68
00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:40.985
And then we throw the herbs in.

69
00:02:40.985 --> 00:02:42.680
Throw the herbs in.
I throw 'em in whole.

70
00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:45.720 line:15%
You can bruise 'em, so you can kinda break 'em if you want.

71
00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:49.190 line:15%
But we like using the whole thing,

72
00:02:49.190 --> 00:02:51.370 line:15%
not taking anything off the stems.

73
00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:53.020 line:15%
And that's it, we just...

74
00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:55.270
Drew, I love you, you're getting in there,

75
00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:56.130
not messing around.
Well,

76
00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:58.105
I wanna love the bird.

77
00:02:58.105 --> 00:03:01.140
The bird is being tenderized

78
00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:02.658
by Drew Barrymore, that's beautiful.

79
00:03:02.658 --> 00:03:04.360
Yeah, it's a baby, I wanna love the bird.

80
00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:07.840
Exactly, this will just sit, essentially, cold-

81
00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:09.194
24 hours?

82
00:03:09.194 --> 00:03:12.680
Even 12 hours would be enough, but 12 to 24 hours

83
00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:14.410
would be plenty enough for this one breast.

84
00:03:14.410 --> 00:03:16.280
And don't exceed 24 hours?

85
00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:18.310
I wouldn't, because then it gets over-salted.

86
00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:19.940 line:15%
And then it like almost keeps

87
00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:21.190 line:15%
all the water in when you're cooking it.

88
00:03:21.190 --> 00:03:22.510 line:15%
Exactly it's the reverse.

89
00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:24.580 line:15%
So instead of when we cut the birds that are coming

90
00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:28.300 line:15%
off the smoker today, it'll be a little more chewy

91
00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:30.640 line:15%
and it won't have the same tenderness and moistness.

92
00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:34.716
It's just like me after a lot of takeout, the next day-

93
00:03:34.716 --> 00:03:35.755
(laughs) Shriveling up.

94
00:03:35.755 --> 00:03:36.588
It's like you could squeeze me,

95
00:03:36.588 --> 00:03:39.167
and it would still just keep coming out of all my pores.

96
00:03:39.167 --> 00:03:40.000
(laughs) I love that.

97
00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:43.070
So that's how the turkey looks going into the brine.

98
00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:44.640
And now we can open the smoker.

99
00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:46.071
Let's see what it looks like.

100
00:03:46.071 --> 00:03:46.904
And then we'll see what they look like cooked, right?

101
00:03:46.904 --> 00:03:49.220 line:15%
And my friend calls me Epcot,

102
00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:51.710 line:15%
because she says I eat like I'm traveling the world.

103
00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:53.380 line:15%
The world, I like that.

104
00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:54.310 line:15%
Can I call you Epcot?

105
00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:55.320 line:15%
Please.
Oh, thank you.

106
00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:56.921 line:15%
That's why I told ya.

107
00:03:56.921 --> 00:03:58.860 line:15%
(laughs) So we're gonna lift this guy up.

108
00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:00.000 line:15%
Wow.

109
00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.650
And we're gonna pull this bad boy out.

110
00:04:02.650 --> 00:04:04.003
Wow.
It's really hot.

111
00:04:05.830 --> 00:04:09.750
And I'm gonna put one of these turkeys on your board.

112
00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:14.750
Wow.
For you, and then-

113
00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:17.070 line:15%
Here, I'm gonna move my brine.

114
00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:20.300 line:15%
I'm gonna put one of these turkeys on here for me.

115
00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:23.920 line:15%
And now we're gonna talk about how do we cut this bad boy.

116
00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:25.870 line:15%
So we're gonna go...

117
00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:29.030 line:15%
Normally we'd start, but what I want you to see the opening.

118
00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:31.300
So we'll go a little further in.

119
00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:33.330
And I kinda like to use my hand as a guide,

120
00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:36.430
and then kinda cut it through there, so.

121
00:04:36.430 --> 00:04:37.460
Wow.

122
00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:42.090
So you could see all the pink around the turkey.

123
00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:46.510
So that's an indication that it was smoked on wood.

124
00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:48.020
All right, so go ahead and cut.

125
00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:49.493
You can cut right into it.

126
00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:52.650
Yeah, it's not gonna be too hot for ya.

127
00:04:53.873 --> 00:04:55.370
There you go, beautiful.

128
00:04:55.370 --> 00:04:56.203
Oh my gosh.

129
00:04:56.203 --> 00:04:58.980
So you see, it's super, super tender.

130
00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:00.440
And then again, you have

131
00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:02.500
these smoke ring we're talking about.

132
00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:04.930
And then, if I just did a little squeeze,

133
00:05:04.930 --> 00:05:07.460
you could see all this beautiful moisture coming.

134
00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:08.950
Wow.
So it's nice

135
00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:11.120
and tender and moist.
Wow.

136
00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:13.810 line:15%
And then it depends, do you like it thicker?

137
00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:14.740 line:15%
Do you like it thinner?

138
00:05:14.740 --> 00:05:16.240 line:15%
What kind of slices do you like?

139
00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:17.170 line:15%
You know, for like

140
00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:20.170 line:15%
a Thanksgiving turkey, I go a little thicker.

141
00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:22.070 line:15%
So like on a sandwich, I like a thinner,

142
00:05:22.070 --> 00:05:24.100 line:15%
but if you're gonna have like Thanksgiving turkey,

143
00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:25.360
a little thicker.
Good, I love it.

144
00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:27.540
It smells like nothing I've ever smelled.

145
00:05:27.540 --> 00:05:28.967
It's so beautiful.

146
00:05:28.967 --> 00:05:30.740
I don't know if this is possible,

147
00:05:30.740 --> 00:05:32.960
but like I can smell the juice.

148
00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:35.490
Perfect, so I'm gonna taste a piece.

149
00:05:35.490 --> 00:05:37.063
Cheers.
Cheers bud.

150
00:05:39.740 --> 00:05:40.573
Oh my gosh.

151
00:05:40.573 --> 00:05:45.390
It's super tender, moist, not over salty,

152
00:05:45.390 --> 00:05:48.800
because we didn't leave it in the brine for too long.

153
00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:53.410
The texture is very, like it's not dry.

154
00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:54.455
No, no.
That's why

155
00:05:54.455 --> 00:05:56.910
it's so delicious.
It's really wet.

156
00:05:56.910 --> 00:05:57.960
Really wet and moist.

157
00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:03.353
I'm happy with it.
That's incredible.

158
00:06:03.353 --> 00:06:04.186
Thank you, bud.

159
00:06:04.186 --> 00:06:05.080
I've never tasted anything like that.

160
00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:05.913
I appreciate that.

161
00:06:05.913 --> 00:06:07.530
I feel bad eating in front of everybody.

162
00:06:07.530 --> 00:06:08.818
This is horrible.

163
00:06:08.818 --> 00:06:10.143
I know, I wanna feed everybody.

164
00:06:11.271 --> 00:06:12.400
Like you said you were so nurturing,

165
00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:14.190
I just wanna start feeding the crew, but I-

166
00:06:14.190 --> 00:06:15.390
I know I do too.

167
00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:17.931
I also have to like try this cornbread.

168
00:06:17.931 --> 00:06:19.143
Wait, wait, wait.

169
00:06:20.670 --> 00:06:22.360
I have to help you with the cornbread, though.

170
00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:24.260
We gotta put honey butter on it, Yeah.

171
00:06:28.590 --> 00:06:31.547
So corn bread, honey butter,

172
00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:34.030
