177
00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:55.860
So Billy, today for Cookbook Club, I wanted to present you

178
00:06:55.860 --> 00:06:58.840
with "The Melon" by Amy Goldman.

179
00:06:58.840 --> 00:06:59.673
Amazing.

180
00:06:59.673 --> 00:07:02.460
What I love about bringing you this book today,

181
00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:07.200
is I think that sometimes you want a little sweetness,

182
00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:09.340
or you want a little freshness,

183
00:07:09.340 --> 00:07:13.260
and I love the way that melon pairs with meat.

184
00:07:13.260 --> 00:07:14.970
Isn't this beautiful?

185
00:07:14.970 --> 00:07:18.420
So this is from my personal collection.

186
00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:22.700
And I just thought, oh, what a great pairing,

187
00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:25.719
barbecue and melons, so I present you-

188
00:07:25.719 --> 00:07:26.552
Well, thank you, my darling.

189
00:07:26.552 --> 00:07:28.313
I actually brought you a book as well.

190
00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:31.210
Two of my great friends from

191
00:07:31.210 --> 00:07:35.000
